From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:55:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_smbx: honour qcom,sw-jeita-enable

Platforms that limit charging by battery temperature in software (the downstream binding's qcom,sw-jeita-enable)
need the PMIC's own JEITA off. On the Surface Duo the PMIC's battery thermistor input reads a bogus hot soft limit
and keeps the charger disabled; Microsoft's downstream DT sets this property and runs JEITA from the two fuel
gauges' temperatures instead.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index 1e2776f14..0ab98fb16 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -970,6 +970,9 @@ static int smb_init_irq(struct smb_chip *chip, int *irq, const char *name,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* JEITA_EN_CFG: bits 4:0 = hard limit + hot/cold soft-limit float-voltage/charge-current compensation */
+#define JEITA_EN_CFG				0x90
+
 static int smb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct power_supply_config supply_config = {};
@@ -1035,6 +1038,17 @@ static int smb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return dev_err_probe(chip->dev, PTR_ERR(chip->chg_psy),
 				     "failed to register power supply\n");
 
+	/*
+	 * qcom,sw-jeita-enable (downstream binding name): the platform limits charging by battery temperature in
+	 * software, so the PMIC's own JEITA must not act. On the Surface Duo the PMIC's battery thermistor input
+	 * reads a bogus hot soft limit and would keep the charger disabled.
+	 */
+	if (of_property_read_bool(chip->dev->of_node, "qcom,sw-jeita-enable")) {
+		rc = regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap, chip->base + JEITA_EN_CFG, 0x1f, 0);
+		if (rc)
+			return dev_err_probe(chip->dev, rc, "failed to disable hardware JEITA\n");
+	}
+
 	rc = power_supply_get_battery_info(chip->chg_psy, &chip->batt_info);
 	if (rc)
 		return dev_err_probe(chip->dev, rc,
